WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.305
To test whether the predicted mass changes are
biologically meaningful,

00:00:04.385 --> 00:00:07.887
the authors compare them against independent measurements.

00:00:07.967 --> 00:00:11.592
Summing NubOT's predicted weights within each
subpopulation,

00:00:11.672 --> 00:00:17.089
they find a strong correlation with the observed
change in cell counts after eight hours,

00:00:17.169 --> 00:00:20.177
with a correlation coefficient of point nine five.

00:00:20.257 --> 00:00:24.191
After twenty-four hours the correlation drops to
point four four,

00:00:24.271 --> 00:00:30.737
because for some drugs the induced cell death is so
severe that too few cells remain to evaluate reliably,

00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:32.837
yet the overall trend still holds.

00:00:32.917 --> 00:00:37.963
Going further, the predicted weights line up
spatially with a proliferation marker,

00:00:38.043 --> 00:00:40.742
Ki67, where NubOT predicts weights above one,

00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:44.757
and with an apoptosis marker where it predicts
weights below one,

00:00:44.837 --> 00:00:50.191
confirming that the model is recovering real
proliferation and death signals rather than

00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:52.600
fitting the distribution superficially.
